---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout title="Material Procurement & Planning" description="A long-range material planning system combining inventory, open customer demand, scheduled receipts, historical consumption, and supplier lead times into purchasing recommendations.">

<section class="case-hero">
  <div class="container">
    <a class="case-back" href="/built-systems/">← Built Systems</a>
    <div class="case-kicker">01 / Materials + Procurement</div>
    <h1>Material Procurement &<br/><em>Planning</em></h1>
    <p class="case-deck">A long-range planning system that combines current inventory, open customer demand, scheduled receipts, historical consumption, and supplier lead times to show what material is needed, how much to buy, and when to act.</p>
    <div class="case-role-line"><span>Demand Planning</span><span>Procurement</span><span>Forecasting</span><span>Data Integration</span><span>Decision Support</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-metrics case-metrics-dark">
  <div class="container case-metric-grid">
    <div><strong>~$3M</strong><span>Material Inventory Scope</span></div>
    <div><strong>18 Months</strong><span>Planning Horizon</span></div>
    <div><strong>20</strong><span>Materials in Portfolio Demo</span></div>
    <div><strong>Weekly</strong><span>Input Update Cycle</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section">
  <div class="container case-two-col">
    <div>
      <div class="case-section-no">01</div><div class="eyebrow">The Planning Problem</div>
      <h2>Long lead times made a current inventory snapshot insufficient.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="case-copy">
      <p>Material purchasing required decisions months before the need reached production. Inventory, purchase orders, customer demand, and consumption history lived in separate sources.</p>
      <p class="case-emphasis">The model brings those signals together to show when coverage becomes tight, what needs to be ordered, and when purchasing should act.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section case-alt section-divider material-input-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">02</div><div class="eyebrow">Planning Model</div>
    <h2>Five inputs become one purchasing view.</h2>
    <div class="input-pipeline">
      <div><small>01</small><strong>Inventory</strong><span>On hand</span></div>
      <div><small>02</small><strong>Customer Demand</strong><span>Need dates</span></div>
      <div><small>03</small><strong>Open Orders</strong><span>Scheduled receipts</span></div>
      <div><small>04</small><strong>Consumption</strong><span>Historical baseline</span></div>
      <div><small>05</small><strong>Supplier Rules</strong><span>Lead time + constraints</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pipeline-output">
      <span>DEMAND + COVERAGE MODEL</span><b>→</b><strong>Risk timing</strong><b>·</b><strong>Order quantity</strong><b>·</b><strong>Purchase date</strong>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section material-demo-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">03</div><div class="eyebrow">Portfolio Demo</div>
    <h2>A decision center for immediate purchasing and long-range coverage.</h2>
    <p class="case-intro">The downloadable workbook uses synthetic material, demand, purchasing, and transaction data. The Planning Hub consolidates the model into a single operating view.</p>

    <div class="material-demo-window">
      <div class="material-demo-bar"><span></span><span></span><span></span><b>Material Planning Hub</b></div>
      <div class="material-demo-body">
        <div class="material-demo-title"><small>DECISION CENTER</small><strong>Immediate orders, customer demand, and 18-month outlook</strong></div>
        <div class="material-kpis">
          <div><span>Materials Covered</span><strong>7</strong></div>
          <div><span>Immediate / Expedite</span><strong>5</strong></div>
          <div><span>Order Within 30 Days</span><strong>0</strong></div>
          <div><span>Suggested New Orders</span><strong>77K lb</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="material-action-table">
          <div class="material-table-head"><span>Material</span><span>Status</span><span>Suggested Order</span><span>Current Inventory</span><span>Open Orders</span><span>18M Forecast</span><span>Confidence</span></div>
          <div class="material-table-row"><span>MTL-004</span><em>EXPEDITE / ORDER NOW</em><span>21.8K lb</span><span>46.5K</span><span>19K</span><span>344K</span><b>48</b></div>
          <div class="material-table-row"><span>MTL-008</span><em>EXPEDITE / ORDER NOW</em><span>22.9K lb</span><span>9.4K</span><span>6K</span><span>73.9K</span><b>59</b></div>
          <div class="material-table-row"><span>MTL-003</span><i>MONITOR</i><span>—</span><span>12.8K</span><span>10K</span><span>34.1K</span><b>89</b></div>
          <div class="material-table-row"><span>MTL-010</span><strong>COVERED</strong><span>—</span><span>7.6K</span><span>32K</span><span>23.9K</span><b>88</b></div>
        </div>
        <div class="material-insight-strip">
          <div><span>Immediate purchasing exposure</span><strong>~77,026 lb across 5 materials</strong></div>
          <div><span>Estimated demo spend</span><strong>~$2.07M in suggested orders</strong></div>
          <div><span>Forecast confidence</span><strong>12 high · 4 medium · 4 low</strong></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="case-note">All quantities, costs, material IDs, and purchasing recommendations shown in the portfolio demo are synthetic.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section case-alt material-action-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">04</div><div class="eyebrow">13-Week Action Planner</div>
    <h2>Turn the forecast into a near-term purchasing board.</h2>
    <p class="case-intro">The rolling 13-week view brings suggested orders and scheduled receipts onto the same weekly timeline, then isolates materials that need buyer attention.</p>
    <div class="action-planner-window">
      <div class="action-planner-head">
        <div><span>Suggested Orders — 13 Weeks</span><strong>77.0K lb</strong></div>
        <div><span>Scheduled Receipts — 13 Weeks</span><strong>68.0K lb</strong></div>
        <div><span>Materials Requiring Action</span><strong>5</strong></div>
      </div>
      <div class="weekly-board">
        <div class="weekly-board-head"><span>Week</span><span>Suggested Orders</span><span>Scheduled Receipts</span><span>Uncovered</span><span>Status</span></div>
        <div><strong>04</strong><span class="bar suggested" style="--w:100%">49.3K</span><span>—</span><span>49.3K</span><b>ACTION NEEDED</b></div>
        <div><strong>05</strong><span class="bar suggested" style="--w:40%">19.6K</span><span>—</span><span>19.6K</span><b>ACTION NEEDED</b></div>
        <div><strong>06</strong><span>—</span><span class="bar scheduled" style="--w:22%">6K</span><span>—</span><em>RECEIPTS ONLY</em></div>
        <div><strong>09</strong><span class="bar suggested" style="--w:17%">8.2K</span><span class="bar scheduled" style="--w:56%">27.5K</span><span>—</span><i>COVERED</i></div>
        <div><strong>10</strong><span>—</span><span class="bar scheduled" style="--w:36%">17.5K</span><span>—</span><em>RECEIPTS ONLY</em></div>
        <div><strong>12</strong><span>—</span><span class="bar scheduled" style="--w:10%">5K</span><span>—</span><em>RECEIPTS ONLY</em></div>
        <div><strong>13</strong><span>—</span><span class="bar scheduled" style="--w:24%">12K</span><span>—</span><em>RECEIPTS ONLY</em></div>
      </div>
      <div class="action-materials">
        <div class="action-materials-head"><span>Material</span><span>Action</span><span>Suggested Order</span><span>Scheduled in Window</span><span>Coverage Check</span></div>
        <div><strong>MTL-004</strong><b>EXPEDITE / ORDER NOW</b><span>21.8K lb</span><span>—</span><em>ORDER / EXPEDITE</em></div>
        <div><strong>MTL-007</strong><b>EXPEDITE / ORDER NOW</b><span>8.2K lb</span><span>7.5K lb</span><em>ORDER / EXPEDITE</em></div>
        <div><strong>MTL-008</strong><b>EXPEDITE / ORDER NOW</b><span>22.9K lb</span><span>—</span><em>ORDER / EXPEDITE</em></div>
        <div><strong>MTL-012</strong><b>EXPEDITE / ORDER NOW</b><span>4.5K lb</span><span>—</span><em>ORDER / EXPEDITE</em></div>
        <div><strong>MTL-016</strong><b>EXPEDITE / ORDER NOW</b><span>19.6K lb</span><span>4K lb</span><em>ORDER / EXPEDITE</em></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="case-note">This website view is based on the workbook’s 13-week purchasing summary and material-action board. Values are synthetic portfolio data.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section material-calendar-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">05</div><div class="eyebrow">Purchasing Calendar</div>
    <h2>Scan down through time and across materials.</h2>
    <p class="case-intro">The workbook’s rolling 52-week calendar keeps weeks on the vertical axis and material types across the columns, so scheduled receipts and suggested orders can be reviewed on the same timeline.</p>
    <div class="purchase-calendar-demo corrected-calendar">
      <div class="calendar-legend"><span><i class="scheduled"></i>Scheduled receipt</span><span><i class="suggested"></i>Suggested order</span></div>
      <div class="vertical-calendar">
        <div class="vcal-row vcal-head"><span>Week</span><span>MTL-004</span><span>MTL-007</span><span>MTL-008</span><span>MTL-010</span><span>MTL-012</span><span>MTL-016</span></div>
        <div class="vcal-row"><strong>W04</strong><span class="suggested">21.8K</span><span></span><span class="suggested">22.9K</span><span></span><span class="suggested">4.5K</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="vcal-row"><strong>W05</strong><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class="suggested">19.6K</span></div>
        <div class="vcal-row"><strong>W06</strong><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class="scheduled">6K</span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <div class="vcal-row"><strong>W09</strong><span></span><span class="suggested">8.2K</span><span></span><span class="scheduled">12K</span><span></span><span class="scheduled">4K</span></div>
        <div class="vcal-row"><strong>W10</strong><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class="scheduled">5.5K</span><span></span><span></span></div>
        <div class="vcal-row"><strong>W12</strong><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class="scheduled">5K</span><span></span></div>
        <div class="vcal-row"><strong>W13</strong><span class="scheduled">8K</span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span></span><span class="scheduled">4K</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="case-note">The website excerpt shows selected materials and weeks for readability; the downloadable workbook carries the full rolling 52-week material matrix.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section case-alt material-horizon-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">06</div><div class="eyebrow">Planning Horizons</div>
    <h2>One model supports decisions from the current quarter through 18 months.</h2>
    <div class="horizon-tabs"><span>Current Quarter</span><span>3 Months</span><span>6 Months</span><span>12 Months</span><span>18 Months</span></div>
    <div class="horizon-visual-grid">
      <div class="horizon-panel">
        <div class="horizon-panel-head"><strong>Near-Term Coverage</strong><span>Current quarter · 3M · 6M</span></div>
        <div class="coverage-mini"><span>MTL-004</span><i class="risk">ORDER</i><span>MTL-008</span><i class="risk">ORDER</i><span>MTL-003</span><i class="watch">MONITOR</i><span>MTL-010</span><i class="ok">COVERED</i></div>
      </div>
      <div class="horizon-panel">
        <div class="horizon-panel-head"><strong>Long-Range Requirement</strong></div>
        <div class="requirement-bars requirement-bars-v2">
          <div class="requirement-header"><span>Material</span><strong>12 Months</strong><strong>18 Months</strong></div>
          <div class="requirement-row"><span>MTL-004</span><div><i style="--w:66%"></i><b>229K</b></div><div><i class="long" style="--w:100%"></i><b>344K</b></div></div>
          <div class="requirement-row"><span>MTL-016</span><div><i style="--w:61%"></i><b>105K</b></div><div><i class="long" style="--w:100%"></i><b>173K</b></div></div>
          <div class="requirement-row"><span>MTL-011</span><div><i style="--w:60%"></i><b>39K</b></div><div><i class="long" style="--w:100%"></i><b>65K</b></div></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="case-note">The workbook provides current-quarter demand alongside 3-period, 6-month, 12-month, and 18-month planning views. Different horizons answer different questions without rebuilding the model.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section material-ownership-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="case-section-no">07</div><div class="eyebrow">Use & Handoff</div>
    <h2>A planning tool with visible assumptions and a clear review point.</h2>
    <div class="compact-governance">
      <div><strong>Procurement</strong><span>Updates receipts and reviews recommended orders.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Operations</strong><span>Maintains assumptions and reviews coverage risk.</span></div>
      <div><strong>Leadership</strong><span>Uses the outlook for spend and long-range exposure.</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="boundary-strip"><span>Safety stock</span><span>Lead time</span><span>Minimum buys</span><span>Yield loss</span><span>Shared supply</span><span>Forecast confidence</span></div>
    <p class="case-note">Recommendations remain planning outputs. Purchasing decisions still account for supplier constraints, changing production conditions, and planner judgment.</p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-section material-download">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="download-card">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Explore the Demo</div>
        <h2>Material Procurement & Planning Dashboard</h2>
        <p>Download the desktop Excel portfolio demo with synthetic inventory, customer demand, scheduled receipts, purchasing calendar, consumption review, planning recommendations, 12- and 18-month forecasts, operational insights, methodology, and instructions.</p>
      </div>
      <a href={`${base}/artifacts/material-procurement-planning-demo.xlsx`} download><span>Download Excel Demo</span><b>↓</b></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<section class="case-next">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="eyebrow">Next System</span>
    <a href="/built-systems/training-certification-system/">
      <strong>Training & Certification System</strong><span>→</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
</BaseLayout>
